Article 6 (Materials to Be Attached to Applications for Permission to Institute Lawsuits)
(1) An organization prescribed in Article 70, subparagraph 1, of the Act shall attach the following materials, etc. to an application for permission to institute a lawsuit:
1. The articles of association of the organization;
2. Materials capable of substantiating that the organization has at least 1,000 regular members;
3. Written materials substantiating the fact that the organization has been registered as a consumer organization under Article 29 of the Act and the date of such registration.
(2) A nationwide economic organization publicly notified by the Minister of Finance and Economy under Article 63 of the Enforcement Decree of the Framework Act on Consumers shall attach to an application for permission to institute a lawsuit a document substantiating that it is such an organization.
(3) An organization prescribed in Article 70, subparagraph 3, of the Act shall attach the following materials, etc. to an application for permission to institute a lawsuit:
1. The articles of association of the organization;
2. Its record of activities during the preceding three years relating to the promotion of consumers' rights and interests, including duties prescribed in Article 28 of the Act;
3. Materials capable of substantiating that the organization has at least 5,000 permanent members;
4. A document substantiating that the organization is registered with a central administrative agency;
5. The names, addresses, and contact information (meaning telephone numbers, facsimile numbers, or electronic mail addresses, etc.; hereinafter the same shall apply) of the consumers who requested the institution of the organization lawsuit;
6. Written requests by the consumers referred to in subparagraph 5 for the institution of the organization lawsuit (each request shall include details of the infringement suffered by the relevant consumer and his or her signature or seal).
(4) An organization instituting a lawsuit shall attach to an application for permission to institute a lawsuit the written request made to the business entity under Article 74 (1) 3 of the Act and the business entity's written opinion thereon. Provided, however, that where the business entity has not responded within 14 days after the written request was made, the business entity's written opinion need not be attached.
